iew_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"API subprocess tests could choose the same port after closing their availability probes and before either child started listening. Cooperating fixtures now hold run-local filesystem leases through startup, restart and child/listener settlement. Exclusive creation of a new generation selects its owner; release moves only that owner's marker, preserving replacement claims and avoiding Windows directory deletion contention. The Windows availability check also covers wildcard listeners.\n\nPart of #407. This changes test infrastructure. Simultaneous independent test runs still require disjoint assigned port ranges; crashed or failed-to-release leases remain reserved until that Vitest run ends.\n\nValidation at `62d443cd2aa321585b45099acb591bf3c24eafaf`:\n- Corrected API coverage: 2,086 passed, 16 declared skips; 95.33% lines, 90.70% branches, 91.59% functions and 93.90% statements. Build, typecheck, lint, dependency layers, dependency-cruiser and formatting passed.\n- Independent actual Claude Code Opus 5.5 xhigh Windows QA: one native two-worker run, 8/8 tests passed. It recorded 979 exclusive grants across 7,270 one-port attempts, 6,291 expected exhaustion refusals, and no unexpected reservation or release errors.\n- Real API checks held the lease before bind, while stopped, after restart and through child close. Foreign listeners survived; stale/replaced markers were preserved; real Windows ACL failures remained visible. All assigned ports were free and the run's reservation root was removed afterward.\n- Initial independent QA found wildcard-listener detection and deletion/contention defects. Both initial failures, the correction evidence and the separate passing Windows QA are retained. The disposable QA harness's four type-only complaints are recorded; candidate typechecking passed.\n- Root verified all 366 archived raw evidence blobs against their staged Git objects and all 13 source/documentation files against the frozen candidate. Most of the diff is this retained evidence.\n\n[Evidence index](https://github.com/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/blob/62d443cd2aa321585b45099acb591bf3c24eafaf/docs/qa/2026-11-17-api-ports-407/README.md) links implementation, original QA, correction and independent correction QA.\n\nNot ready to merge. Current-head/current-target CI remains pending. The first [hosted POSIX control](https://github.com/Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin/actions/runs/44251885185) confirmed a macOS wildcard-listener defect at this head: 11/13 maintained cases and 1/2 independent witness cases passed, while occupied IPv4/IPv6 wildcard ports were incorrectly granted. Linux passed 13/13 and 2/2. A bounded Darwin probe correction is underway; fresh native verification is required. The IPv6-unavailable fallback has controlled-fault evidence, not a native unavailable-IPv6 run. Opposite-family Claude formal review and fresh independent Astra MAX final audit remain pending, with 0/3 formal scans consumed. The #503 audit blocker remains in force.","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-18T06:21:15Z","updated_at":"2026-11-18T06:37:04Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"ce8c365d70a221ea358b8c96a7f638a541d0e000","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"Jacob-J-Thomas:codex/gg-20261117-ports-407","ref":"codex/gg-20261117-ports-407","repo":{"id":1403707890,"node_id":"R_kgDOU6rh8g","name":"GraphGoblin","full_name":"Jacob-J-Thomas/GraphGoblin","owner":{"login":"Jacob-J-Thomas","id":92639671,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYWRtw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92639671?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jacob-J-Thomas","html_url":"https://github.com/Jacob-J-Thomas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jacob-J-Thomas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jacob-J-Thomas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/use